  "fidelity_notes": [
    "finding: The sentences connect nanotwin networks to increased strength and ductility, but do not mention toughness or the full claimed strength–ductility–toughness combination.",
    "finding: The sentence applies this mechanism to BCC pure metals and dilute BCC alloys, not specifically to BCC non-dilute and high-entropy alloys.",
    "finding: The sentence supports balanced strength and ductility in eutectic alloys, but does not state that the alloys are bulk, near-eutectic, or effective over a wide temperature range.",
    "finding: The sentence identifies the γ′ phase but does not explicitly state nickel-base superalloys.",
    "finding: The conclusion concerns the citing authors’ own HEAs and is not attributed to the cited work.",
    "finding: The sentence supports use of partial recrystallization and bimodal grains, but not the added claims about cryogenic strengthening and room-temperature twinning; it presents a comparison.",
    "finding: The sentence discusses stacking faults and dynamic Hall–Petch hardening, not heterogeneous-structure enhancement of the strength–ductility trade-off or an explicitly identified HEA.",
    "compares: The sentence compares corrosion results in specified high-entropy alloys, not corrosion mechanisms in casing.",
    "compares: The citing paper’s heterogeneous structure is said to have strength similar to the cited uniform-UFG MEA; the comparison itself is not a finding attributed to the cited work.",
    "compares: The sentence uses nanocrystalline W as a mechanical-property comparator but does not mention an irradiation-resistance grain-size threshold or ultrafine tungsten.",
    "compares: The sentence identifies the comparison only as involving three H/MEAs and does not name CrCoNi.",
    "compares: The sentence specifies MoS2/NF, not the broader description “MoS2 with Multifunctional Active Sites.”"
  ],
